cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or scripts, please cite them as below, together with the manuscript."
title: "autonima-paper: configurations, results and meta-analytic maps for the AutoNIMA manuscript"
abstract: >-
  Project configurations, pipeline outputs (screening decisions, parsed
  coordinates, analysis selections, NiMADS studysets), evaluation tables,
  figure and number scripts, and the meta-analytic maps behind the manuscript
  "Automated neuroimaging meta-analysis through LLM-guided selection improves
  recovery of published spatial patterns". Maps were generated with AutoNIMA
  v0.1.1 on NiMARE 0.21.0 and are distributed as maps.tar.gz.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/neurostuff/autonima-paper"
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - meta-analysis
  - large language models
  - systematic review
  - NiMARE
